WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.255
The takeaway: infinite-pixel synthesis becomes
tractable once you stop tying generation to a fixed resolution.

00:00:07.335 --> 00:00:09.389
By separating global appearance,

00:00:09.469 --> 00:00:13.257
local structure via a coordinate-driven implicit function,

00:00:13.337 --> 00:00:15.991
and texture via a padding-free generator,

00:00:16.071 --> 00:00:20.993
InfinityGAN produces patches that are independent
yet perfectly consistent,

00:00:21.073 --> 00:00:26.061
tiling into images of any size at constant memory
and generated in parallel.

00:00:26.141 --> 00:00:30.929
The same framework unlocks spatial style fusion,
multi-modal outpainting,

00:00:31.009 --> 00:00:34.530
and arbitrary-length panoramas, all from tiny patches.
